judge_raw_output:
The analyzer shows a clear sign the optimizer chased nonzero exploration objectives (distance_from_center mean=0.4046, weight=0.4; parameter_spread mean=0.3856, weight=0.2) while performance was 0.0 for all 32 candidates (mean=0.0, std=0.0). The simplest, highest-leverage fix is to make performance the dominant objective so the optimizer must seek nonzero performance and thereby reveal whether the performance scorer is responsive.

<decision>
{
  "failure_location": "objective",
  "root_cause_hypothesis": "The performance objective was effectively not weighted (weight=None) while distance_from_center (weight=0.4) and parameter_spread (weight=0.2) provided nonzero feedback; the optimizer prioritized those signals and ignored performance, producing high exploration but no performance improvement.",
  "intervention_target": "objective",
  "rationale": "Performance is 0.0 for all 32 candidates (mean=0.0, std=0.0, best=0.0) while distance_from_center mean=0.4046 (best=0.4858) and parameter_spread mean=0.3856 (best=0.4856). This pattern indicates the optimizer followed the nonzero objectives. For a quick diagnostic and to force the search to reveal whether the performance scorer works, make performance the dominant/sole objective.",
  "proposed_change": {
    "ops": [
      {"op": "set_weight", "name": "performance", "weight": 1.0},
      {"op": "drop", "name": "distance_from_center"},
      {"op": "drop", "name": "parameter_spread"}
    ]
  },
  "expected_benefit": "Forces the optimizer to focus on maximizing measured performance; if the performance scorer is functioning, we should see nonzero performance values quickly. If performance remains zero, this isolates the problem to the evaluator rather than objective weighting, preventing further wasted exploration.",
  "validation_plan": "Run the next iteration with the updated objectives. Success is indicated by any candidate achieving performance > 0 (nonzero mean or best > 0) within the next iteration(s). If performance remains 0 across the population, treat as evaluator/scorer failure and halt to diagnose measurement.",
  "confidence": 0.8
}
</decision>

Rationale (brief): Analyzer shows near-total stagnation: 32 candidates, best performance = 0.0002, rest = 0.0, published mean/std effectively 0.0000 ± 0.0000. This suggests the optimizer is sampling a region where the performance scorer returns near-zero values (low informational signal). Adding a single exploration-oriented objective that encourages movement away from the central region is the least intrusive, high-leverage change. distance_from_center directly rewards moving away from (0.5,...,0.5), which the Analyzer flagged as a likely dead zone; a modest weight will nudge the search toward boundary regions where performance may be nonzero without completely overriding performance optimization.

<decision>
{
  "failure_location": "objective",
  "root_cause_hypothesis": "The current objective landscape appears insensitive around the sampled region (centered designs), producing near-zero performance for almost all candidates; optimizer lacks exploration pressure to escape this likely dead zone (hypothesis uncertain).",
  "intervention_target": "objective",
  "rationale": "32 candidates evaluated with best performance = 0.0002 and most = 0.0 (Analyzer). Adding distance_from_center (registered scorer) as a second objective will encourage moving away from the center (0.5,...,0.5), which the Analyzer specifically recommended and is the most direct single-objective way to promote exploration toward regions that may yield nonzero performance. Use a modest weight so performance remains primary.",
  "proposed_change": {
    "ops": [
      {
        "op": "add_from_registry",
        "name": "distance_from_center",
        "optimization_direction": "maximize",
        "weight": 0.10
      }
    ]
  },
  "expected_benefit": "Increased exploration away from the central dead zone should produce greater diversity in sampled designs and increase the chance of finding candidates with nonzero performance, providing more informative gradients for the optimizer.",
  "validation_plan": "Run the next optimization iteration(s) with the added objective and check whether the best or mean performance improves relative to the current state (best=0.0002, mean≈0.0). The independent validator will accept the change if it yields an improvement in the accepted metric(s). Monitor also whether population distance_from_center increases, confirming the exploration effect.",
  "confidence": 0.60
}
</decision>

The population is optimizing the exploration objectives while the primary objective is uniformly zero (performance mean=0.0000, std=0.0000, best=0.0000). distance_from_center has increased (mean=0.3896, +0.0048) and parameter_spread increased (mean=0.3732, +0.0059), showing optimizer is following secondary objectives. Hypothesis: either the performance scorer is failing or the performance signal is extremely sparse; in either case the exploration objectives are masking any small performance signal. A minimal, targeted objective-level intervention is the best next step: remove the exploration objectives so any nonzero performance signal will drive selection (and also set an explicit weight for performance).

