The analyzer shows an effectively flat performance signal (mean 0.0000, std 0.0002, best 0.0011), consistent with either a scorer failure or universally near-zero device performance. Because continuing with only the silent performance objective will stall selection, the next best conservative step is to add an exploration objective that produces a reliable, non-degenerate signal so the optimizer can meaningfully differentiate candidates while the recommended diagnostic is run. This is a single, bounded objective-level change.

